From 91f6b63c36c5739d540ad3462b00d639e042c008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:24:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(kernel): a machining mesh from solidcore-tess with a
 measured deviation

A solidcore-imported STEP solid is meshed by solidcore-tess at a chord in
mm and handed out only whole and measured inside the tolerance:
- every PlanStats shortfall that touches the guarantee (unmeshed, lenient,
  unsampled edge, a face or edge capped off its tolerance) and every
  evaluator refusal is a named MeshRefusal; the rest are report notes;
- the deviation is sampled at 15 barycentric points a triangle, against
  the plan surface at the same (u, v) and against the record face's
  analytic surface in closed form; judged by the analytic distance where
  the face is analytic, else the parametric one;
- welded by exact position: no open, over-shared or turned side; positive
  volume; the app's 30 M triangle budget; a tolerance under a millionth
  of the body is refused, never quietly coarsened; a CancelToken bound.

StepSolid keeps its reader record. solidcore-tess moves from a dev- to a
library dependency of the kernel (no new package); wasm32 checks clean.
Bench (kernel release lane): every fixture within 0.005 and 0.01 mm;
truck stands 9.99e-3 mm off on the metre file at the 0.005 cap.
Decisions in docs/decisions/940-machining-mesh.md; follow-up #1029.

